cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this framework, please cite the manuscript and the archived release."
title: "Actor-role components of dyadic event forecasts: exact attribution and a portability audit"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible framework and public artifact for actor-role components of
  binary dyad-month political event forecasts: exact additive attribution into
  source-role, target-role, dyad and non-actor groups, plus a portability audit.
  The confirmatory evaluation is a pre-registered, one-shot, unit-fresh 20%
  dyad holdout; it is retrospective, not time-fresh. The stability audit is
  provisional, holdout-excluded and based on 50 dyad-cluster bootstrap refits;
  it is not a holdout-side stability test. The public experiment scripts are a
  five-seed preview of the audit method and do not regenerate the 50-refit
  holdout-excluded aggregates. Source code is MIT-licensed; ICEWS-derived
  aggregate results are not MIT and remain under the ICEWS research-and-teaching
  terms. This is a v0.1.1 release candidate: the v0.1.1 git tag and the DOI are
  pending.
authors:
  - name: "LAGS-1 authors"
version: "0.1.1"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - dyadic event forecasting
  - ICEWS
  - explainability
  - stability audit
  - calibration
  - reproducibility
repository-code: "https://github.com/Quietpeng/lags1-dyad-explanations"
